    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d287">

                <pb facs="0397" n="329" xml:id="pg329"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">841.711/1590½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Wilson to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-11-26">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">26 November, 1916</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I fear it was a little
                    stupid in me not to perceive the real character of this memorandum.<anchor
                        n="17" xml:id="d287-f1"/> Thank you for correcting me.</p>
                <p>The argument and the position seem to me all right, and I hope that you will
                    prepare our note in reply to the British along these lines. I shall be
                    interested to go over it with you when you shall have completed it.</p>
                <p>Faithfully Yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. W.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
